id: pm-github-vhi6
title: Bound coverage aggregation memory and compare default-heap CI behavior
description: "During the PR #122 privacy-scope regression work, an identity-isolated npm release:check completed 587/587 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations, then c8 report aggregation exhausted Node's default 4 GiB heap. Native coverage receipts occupied approximately 2.9 GiB. The security fix is being validated with NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=12288 and unchanged source inventory and four 100-percent thresholds. Compare default-heap CI behavior, investigate bounded report aggregation or documented resource requirements, and retain complete authored-source and real CLI coverage. Earlier local heap-exhaustion observations also appear in pm-github-fmrf; this task tracks current default-heap acceptance separately from the scope fix in pm-github-wrmt."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: coverage,follow-up,gates
created_at: "2026-10-14T14:32:34.672Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T19:41:18.480Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T15:04:27.090Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed resource workaround: complete identity-isolated npm and Bun release:check each passed 587/587 tests and all 11 checks with NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=12288. Coverage remains exact 100/100/100/100 across 12 authored modules, without source exemptions or threshold changes. The earlier default-heap npm run passed all 587 tests before c8 aggregation exhausted the heap. Default-heap CI comparison and bounded aggregation remain follow-up work; the security change does not alter coverage implementation or CI memory settings."
  "2026-10-24T14:34:24.911Z",codex-agent,"Additional measured receipt from pm-github-closeout-attribution / PR 174: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40101464708 at 30b94f1 failed all four npm/Bun release jobs on Node 22/26 with JavaScript heap exhaustion during c8 aggregation at the existing 8192 MiB limit. The Node 26 test phases each passed 1337/1337, zero failures/cancellations/skips before aggregation failed. No release-gate pass is claimed. This round reduces repeated setup in the new 36-case workflow matrix (shared immutable Git/tracker baselines and only the actual closeout/publication steps); the broader bounded aggregation task remains open, with thresholds, source inventory and heap configuration unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T15:10:00.744Z",codex-agent,"Second receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40103921945 at ad2e7cb passed 1337/1337 tests in every npm/Bun Node 22/26 job, then all four c8 aggregations exhausted the unchanged 8192 MiB heap. Sharing tracker callers alone was insufficient while package setup still repeated per cell. The next harness prepares package/scope setup once per immutable baseline; every one of the 36 cases still restores input, runs actual branch preparation, real CLI closeout, publication privacy/refusal gates and leased push, with fresh receipts and provenance/history assertions. No coverage resource or threshold change is used. The broader bounded aggregation task remains open."
  "2026-10-24T15:38:04.069Z",codex-agent,"Third CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40106191758 at cff0f1c passed the complete npm release gate on Node 22 after preparing four baseline callers once. Both Node 26 jobs still passed 1337/1337 tests and exhausted c8 at 8192 MiB. Fixture reductions alone cannot establish Node 26 full-gate acceptance. Adjust only the c8 merge heap ceiling to 12288 MiB, leaving headroom on this public repository's documented 16 GB ubuntu-latest runners (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/github-hosted-runners#standard-github-hosted-runners-for-public-repositories). All four coverage thresholds remain 100, the complete 19-module inventory, zero-exclusion policy, test set and dependency pins stay unchanged. Earlier comments preserving the 8 GiB ceiling describe failed earlier attempts; measured Node 26 failures now justify this resource-only revision. General bounded aggregation remains unfinished and this item will not be closed."
  "2026-10-24T15:42:23.333Z",codex-agent,"Resource-only local verification: PM-linked node --test test/coverage-gate.test.ts passes 9/9, zero failures/cancellations/skips. These tests run real c8 fixture reports and preserve threshold-refusal, missing-source, invalid-receipt and pre-entry heap-routing controls. Production typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. Only COVERAGE_HEAP_FLAG changes from 8192 to 12288 MiB, plus explanatory comments. Full CI is still required; this is not bounded-memory certification and the general task stays in progress for orchestrator follow-up."
  "2026-10-24T21:53:34.277Z",codex-agent,"Returned to open in the 2026-10-24 sweep: PR 174 reduces fixture duplication and raises the c8 heap limit, but explicitly leaves bounded coverage aggregation unfinished. No active work."
  "2026-11-02T13:08:38.050Z",codex-sol,"Additional #175 gate receipt: the expanded 1609-case full suite reached c8 aggregation, which exhausted the unchanged 12288 MiB cap. Test failures were separately corrected on pm-github-repeat-noop; no gate pass is claimed from this attempt. Checking an operational NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=60 override, which Node documents as taking precedence over the explicit absolute cap. No source inventory, threshold, exclusion, assertion or checked-in heap default is changed; bounded/default-cap aggregation remains open."
  "2026-11-02T13:17:42.367Z",codex-sol,"Resource probe completed successfully: c8 can aggregate the retained first-attempt native receipts with NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=60, preserving the checked-in 12288 MiB argument. This is only a memory-capacity probe, not corrected-source coverage certification: the retained run had three test failures and source changed afterwards. A new complete release:check now reruns all tests and exact four-dimensional 100-percent gates with that operational override. No gate source or assertion changes. Default-cap CI/resource acceptance remains open."
  "2026-11-02T17:44:18.578Z",codex-sol,"Continuation resource receipt for #175: fresh complete release:check now exits 0 with operational NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=60. Tests 1609/1609, exact 100/100/100/100 across 28 authored modules (13197 lines/statements, 422 functions, 5075 branches), zero skipped source. The checked-in 12288 MiB ceiling and all gate thresholds/exclusions remain unchanged. This demonstrates current-source local acceptance with the operational override only; bounded aggregation and default-cap CI remain unresolved. Item stays open."
  "2026-11-02T18:04:23.766Z",codex-sol,"Related verification receipt: pm-github-01n8. A complete 1609-test Node run reached 1607 passes and two candidate fixture failures, then c8 aggregation exhausted the configured 12 GiB heap before producing coverage receipts. This extends the existing aggregation-memory follow-up; no duplicate item is created. The fixture assertions are being preserved and repaired separately. A bounded 16 GiB heap diagnostic uses the saved raw receipts with the same authored-source inventory and four 100-percent thresholds. No successful default-heap or CI result is claimed."
  "2026-11-02T18:25:45.106Z",codex-sol,"The saved-receipt diagnostic completed with a bounded 16 GiB heap: all 29 authored modules, exact 13776/13776 lines and statements, 437/437 functions, 5184/5184 branches, zero skips. This does not turn the failed test attempt into a passing release gate. The complete command will be rerun after the two fixture repairs pass, with a resource-only heap override and unchanged inventory/thresholds. Default-cap and CI acceptance remain separate, unproven claims."
  "2026-11-02T19:41:18.479Z",codex-sol,"The related privacy candidate completed a fresh release:check successfully: 1609/1609 tests, all 29 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100, zero skipped source, all later release checks passed. It used NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=55 (verified effective heap limit 17805 MiB) after the 12 GiB-cap attempt exhausted its heap. The independent 16 GiB report and fresh larger-heap run agree on exact counters. This item stays open for bounded/default-cap and CI acceptance; local profile success does not establish those results."
